00:10:08.120 --> 00:10:10.300
What if you're using
some other language--

00:10:10.300 --> 00:10:14.650
Rust or Ruby-- or what if you
have additional requirements

00:10:14.650 --> 00:10:17.480
beyond just 100 lines of code?

00:10:17.480 --> 00:10:20.230
Maybe you do have some
system level dependencies.

00:10:20.230 --> 00:10:22.660
Maybe you're interacting
with robotics

00:10:22.660 --> 00:10:25.690
so you need the Robot Operating
System available to you.

00:10:25.690 --> 00:10:28.100
Maybe you need access
to different things.

00:10:28.100 --> 00:10:31.150
And this is why we introduced
Cloud Run just a few weeks ago

00:10:31.150 --> 00:10:32.560
at Google Cloud Next.

00:10:32.560 --> 00:10:37.030
Cloud Run is the latest edition
of our server offerings.

00:10:37.030 --> 00:10:38.560
Remember, we talk
about serverless.

00:10:38.560 --> 00:10:40.570
We mean don't
manage any servers,

00:10:40.570 --> 00:10:42.430
don't install any packages.

00:10:42.430 --> 00:10:45.310
With Cloud Run, you
package your application

00:10:45.310 --> 00:10:48.670
and all of its dependencies into
this thing called a container

00:10:48.670 --> 00:10:50.080
or a docker container.

00:10:50.080 --> 00:10:54.070
And then Cloud Run scales
that container for you

00:10:54.070 --> 00:10:55.580
automatically.

00:10:55.580 --> 00:10:58.540
You run the gcloud command
to deploy your function

00:10:58.540 --> 00:10:59.770
to Cloud Run.

00:10:59.770 --> 00:11:02.650
Cloud Run will automatically
scale your function,

00:11:02.650 --> 00:11:04.900
and it will even
scale it down to zero.

00:11:04.900 --> 00:11:06.400
And this is very
important if you're

00:11:06.400 --> 00:11:08.590
an early stage startup or
a mid-sized company that's

00:11:08.590 --> 00:11:09.670
tight on a budget.

00:11:09.670 --> 00:11:11.500
Because with Cloud
Functions and Cloud Run,

00:11:11.500 --> 00:11:15.370
you will only pay while
your code is being run.

00:11:15.370 --> 00:11:18.825
You don't pay if no one is
accessing that endpoint.

00:11:18.825 --> 00:11:20.950
And if all of a sudden you
have a million users who

00:11:20.950 --> 00:11:22.660
are all accessing
that endpoint, we'll

00:11:22.660 --> 00:11:24.640
scale for you automatically.

00:11:24.640 --> 00:11:26.920
And we'll automatically
scale back down

00:11:26.920 --> 00:11:28.570
when that traffic alleviates.

00:11:31.770 --> 00:11:33.630
That's code for you.

